narchy  instead of questioning how shuri's  tactics will affect the average wakandan  they simply on the Midnight Angel armor  as an upgrade and a Hail Mary support of  her plans but to be fair to these  changes wakanda forever is simply the  introduction of the midnight angels and  they'll have plenty of time to explore  their key role in wakandan politics down  the line while I don't think that the  MCU will ever fully have the midnight  Angels turn on shuri or the newly  implied King Baku I do think that  they'll be instrumental in exploring the  grayer areas of wakandan society and  ultimately play a part in reshaping the  political structure of the nation the  country of wakanda Simply isn't at the  same point it was in the comics when the  midnight Angels were necessary to  liberate the people but it is getting  there only kind of in Reverse instead of  losing civilians to Doctor Doom then  name more than the black order then  Civil War the MCU saw killmonger's coup  followed by the black orders invasion of  wakanda and lastly anymore's flood If  This truly is supposed to mirror the  comics Doom has to be next I know I'm  not alone in expecting Dr Doom and his  quest for vibranium as a future plot  point in the MCU and seeing that the  initial midnight Angels were formed to  assassinate Doom I think it's fair to  expect these forces to collide in a  breaking point for wakandans to me it's  no coincidence that Midnight Angel Okoye  is the final connection to Everett  Ross's subplot within wakanda forever  not saying that Val is Dr Doom but her  and Ross's entire portion of the movie  is a setup for a foreign government's  plan to infiltrate and seize wakanda's  resources this is exactly what Doom did  during doommore the US government is  already working on joint operations to  acquire vibranium so it wouldn't be  far-fetched to assume that Val might  align with lot various Doctor Doom in  order to get her hands on some of that  precious metal even without Doom